For `line` type: `serie.stroke = colorFn` — a function `(u, idx) => s._focus === false ? s.getFocusedColor(y, idx) : s[field]` where `s[field]` = `u.series[idx].color`. uPlot calls `stroke` function at draw time, reading `u.series[idx].color`. So if I update `color` via `setSeries(id, {color: newColor})` — UPDATE_KEYS includes `color` → assignKeys copies `color` into `this.uplot.series[seriesIdx].color`. Then a redraw will paint with the new color. 

So on theme change:
```ts
chart.setTheme(theme);
chart.setSeries('cpu', {color: getComputedStyle…});
chart.redraw(true, false);
```

