events.content:
One more subtle issue: in the theme effect, `chart.setSeries(SERIES_ID, {...})` — inside `_setSeries`, for the id-string path:

```js
if (['number', 'string'].includes(typeof timelineOrSeriesOrId)) {
    useIncremental = false;
    useFullyRedraw = false;
    series = [maybeSeries];
    updateId = timelineOrSeriesOrId;
}
```

Then `matched = this.config.series.find(({id}) => id === serie.id || id === updateId)` → serie.id undefined, updateId 'cpu' → matched ✓. `if (matched && id)` ✓. `const {data, ...rest} = serie` — data undefined; rest = {color, lineColor}. `useIncremental` false → `else if (data?.length)` — data undefined → skip, shouldRecalcData stays false ✓. `configureSeries(this, Object.assign(matched, rest), seriesIdx)` — re-parses colors ✓. assignKeys UPDATE_KEYS (width, pointsSize, color, lineColor, lineWidth, $c) → uOpts.color and uOpts.lineColor updated ✓. 

For area type, `stroke = getSerieFocusColors(yagr, 'lineColor')` → reads `u.series[idx].lineColor` at draw ✓. `fill = colorFn` reads `u.series[idx].color` ✓. So after `chart.redraw(true, ...)`, the fill and stroke repaint with new colors. ✓

One concern: `shouldUpdateCursror = true` when color changes → cursor.updatePoints() ✓ fine.

Now — `chart.setTheme(theme)` is called first, which triggers `wrapBatch(() => () => this.redraw(false, true))`... wait:

```js
setTheme(themeValue) {
    this.utils.theme.setTheme(themeValue);
    ...classList...
    if (!this.uplot) return;
    this.wrapBatch(() => () => this.redraw(false, true));
}
```
wrapBatch with a non-array res: `const [fnsOrFn, shouldRecalc] = Array.isArray(res) ? res : [res, false]` → fns = [fn] → uplot.batch(() => fn()) → redraw(false, true). ✓

Then my setSeries + redraw(true, true) repaints series too. Order fine.

`utils.theme.setTheme` — ThemedDefaults.setTheme flips theme-dependent getters (DEFAULT_LINE_COLOR, SHIFT...) ✓.

Another check — the `x` axis: I didn't configure axes.x; yagr creates default time axis. Values like "12:00". With locale ru. ✓

Edge: on unmount, `emitStats` might fire after dispose? No — interval cleared first, dispose after. ✓ StrictMode: mount1 → cleanup1 → mount2. During cleanup1 chart1.dispose() removes its canvas DOM from root. Then mount2 creates chart2 fresh. ✓

What about `adaptive` ResizeObserver when root has flex sizing: initial size at construction — uPlot gets width/height from clientWidth/Height at init. In preview/prod the div is laid out before effects run (effects run after DOM insertion & layout? Effects run after render commit but before paint; layout is computed — clientHeight available ✓).

Now, App.tsx — one check: `Card view="filled"` — valid? Card view options in uikit 7: 'clear' | 'filled' | 'raised' — ✓. size="l" ✓.

`Switch` `onUpdate` — ✓ has that prop.

Also check `Text variant="header-1"` exists: variants: 'header-1', 'header-2', 'subheader-1..3', 'body-1..3', 'caption-1..2' ✓.

`Icon data={Sun} size={16}` ✓.

One a11y nit: `role="img"` on interactive chart — it's interactive (zoom/hover). Better: remove role or use figure semantics. Let me change to `role="figure"`? There's no role="figure"... there IS `role="figure"` in ARIA 1.1. Hmm — for interactivity, honestly plain div with aria-label on group role: `role="group"` with aria-label. Let me use role="group"... Actually simplest accessible: keep aria-label, drop role (divs are generic; aria-label on generic div without role is ignored). Use `role="figure"` + aria-label — valid ARIA role, non-interactive semantics but doesn't block interaction. Hmm, role="img" would make AT treat children as presentational which could hide the tooltip content from AT. Tooltip is mouse-driven anyway.

I'll switch to role="figure". Minor.

Also `html lang="ru"` ✓ already in index.html.

Cleanup: kill the preview server background task (b4ko89nho still running), remove /tmp/shot. Actually leaving /tmp is fine, but kill the server.

